      "writtenOn": "2021-06-04T02:01:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The page is obtained from the origin path at the first time, the page is doing a get_page() there.\n\nThen after the page is put in the cache, we mark the pointer `page` to NULL, this will prevent the page being freed by the put_page() at line 2874. And this is why we use the \"struct page**\".\n\nThe put_page() will be called when we foud the cached page not valid with the fault page in the first hook for the next page fault.\n\nSo, we didn\u0027t do a extra get_page() in this hook, instead, we prevent the put_page at line 2847 to be called. Maybe I should change the code to do a get_page() like you suggest, which would be more clear.",
